WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.814
Deploying a detection is an operational change.

2
00:00:02.814 --> 00:00:10.537
Teams should consider whether the detection will alert immediately, whether it should run silently first, and who will monitor early behavior.

3
00:00:10.537 --> 00:00:18.678
A rollout should also define which playbook applies, how analysts will interpret the signal, and how unexpected alert volume will be handled.

4
00:00:18.678 --> 00:00:20.924
Careful deployment reduces surprise.

5
00:00:20.924 --> 00:00:26.571
It gives teams a chance to understand real-world behavior before relying on the detection fully.

6
00:00:26.571 --> 00:00:28.956
Managed rollout also supports trust.

7
00:00:28.956 --> 00:00:36.948
Analysts are more likely to use a new detection well when they understand its purpose, severity, expected context, and escalation path.
